\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. One there is above all others,
\par Well deserves the name of friend;
\par His is love beyond a brother's,
\par Costly, free, and knows no end:
\par They who once His kindness prove,
\par Find it everlasting love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Which of all our friends, to save us,
\par Could or would have shed his blood?
\par But our Jesus died to have us
\par Reconciled in Him to God:
\par This was boundless love indeed;
\par Jesus is a friend in need.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When He lived on earth abased,
\par Friend of sinners was His name;
\par Now above all glories raised;
\par He rejoices in the same;
\par Still He calls them brethren, friends,
\par And to all their wants attends.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O for grace our hearts to soften!
\par Teach us, Lord, at length to love;
\par We, alas! forget too often
\par What a friend we have above;
\par But when home our souls are brought,
\par We shall love Thee as we ought.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

